{"metadata":{"name":"Sunan Abu Dawud","section":{"15":{"eng-name":"Jihad (Kitab Al-Jihad)","ara-name":"كتاب الجهاد"}},"section_detail":{"15":{"hadithnumber_first":2477,"hadithnumber_last":2787,"arabicnumber_first":2477,"arabicnumber_last":2787}}},"hadiths":[{"hadithnumber":2486,"arabicnumber":2486,"text":"Rapporté par Abu Umamah رضي الله عنه : « Un homme a dit : “Messager d’Allah, permets-moi de voyager pour l’adoration.” Le Prophète ﷺ a répondu : “Le voyage de ma communauté, c’est de lutter dans le chemin d’Allah, le Très-Haut.” »","grades":[{"name":"Al-Albani","grade":"Hasan"},{"name":"Muhammad Muhyi Al-Din Abdul Hamid","grade":"Hasan"},{"name":"Zubair Ali Zai","grade":"Isnaad Hasan"}],"reference":{"book":15,"hadith":10},"chapter":{"id":6,"ara-name":"باب فِي النَّهْىِ عَنِ السِّيَاحَةِ","eng-name":"Regarding The Prohibition Of Wandering (As-Siyahah)","isFirstHadith":true}}]}